    "turn_text": "Outkick 360 continues across the Outkick Network, the crew wall here at 50 Peabody in Nashville. We'll get back to more college football and NFL discussion on the field coming up later this hour. The discussion over the last year or so, guys, has been name, image, license, office field. We know that Commissioner Stanky, Paul, you and I chatted with him on SEC media days. He was on Capitol Hill recently meeting with senators, meeting with those in the house, and trying to come up with an idea and a structure of what federal legislation might look like. We have Senator Tommy Tuberville on the line, former head coach at Auburn at Ole Miss, Cincinnati and Texas Tech. And now he is fronting a bipartisan legislation to help try to get us down the path of guardrails for name, image, likeness. Coach Tuberville, great to have you on. Good morning. How are y'all? We are very well. And you did tell us, hey, still calling me coach. I appreciate that.",
