  {
    "episode_id": 65052,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/5/65052.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "Well, you know, just talking to coaches back in the summer, you know, I would call some my friends of mine that were head coaches or assistants and knowing that in the month of May, you know, you're out and evaluating players going to high schools, talking to coaches, watching players practice and spring, spring practice, all those things. And I'm calling them going, Hey, where are you at today? I'm raising money or what? You're not recruiting? No, we got to raise money. And it's kind of dawned on me where we've gone with this. When you've got coaches that's roughly done the right thing for high school players and high school coaches that instead of evaluations and given people opportunities to earn scholarships, they have to raise the money to try to pay some only just a few of the top players. And the other one is, the other thing that really upset me was coaches talking about, we're gonna cut back on on signing high school players. That's what he's talking about. Well, you know, we're going to build our football team off of transfers because of transfer portal. So we're going to start working on transfers. We're not going to sign 25, we might sign 10, and we're going to take 15 transfers. So what you're doing now is you're eliminating opportunities for high school kids that worked all their life to try to get that football scholarship. You're limiting the potential percentage of what we used to have from, you know, say 100% of the high school athletes signed, everybody has 25 to possibly 60 to 70, even 50% of the past recruits that you had signed, instead of taking high school kids, you're gonna take transfers. And so that bothered me because I know the opportunities that kids have when they go to college. have their scholarship played for it and get a good education. They worked away up. They learned leadership. They learned how to play with other people. Now you're going to potentially cut a lot of those people out. That's not what this country was built on.",
