    "turn_text": "Yeah, Joe and I talked about this. And I think that's one thing. Yeah, I have to do. We know really very little about some of these collectives. And we're going to either try to get some come here to Washington DC where we can set down and let them explain their programs to us, get their ideas, the good and the bad. You're going to need these groups because I want to get coaches out of raising money. I mean, that's absolutely ridiculous. They don't need to be doing that. They need to be spending time with the players, athletes, training, working on their education. When they're out there raising money, that is the wrong message that we're sending to college sports. If people don't handle money, it should be the collectives or somebody likes the collectives. Again, I don't know enough about those yet, but I'll tell you here in a few months, I'm going to be an expert on it. But I'm going to learn from them. I want to hear their thoughts. Obviously, they're going to make money out of it. I'm fine with that. But I'm also going to make sure that these student athletes are taken care of, not lied to, not taken advantage of. That is the sole purpose of what we're trying to do through this whole process. So, again, they're the There's a lot of things out there. You've got no job in talking about it. I'm sure almost every day for the last year and have some degree. But at the end of the day, we need fairness for all schools, big universities, and small universities. And we can get the fairness for that. I think we can accomplish something here. And again, it might take some tweaking as we go along, but we've got to have a base where to start. And before we put this so-called future bill, in front of the Congress and President of the United States, we want to make sure that it's the proper thing to do, and it will have an opportunity to work and make it fair for all.",
