    "turn_text": "Well, again, there's going to be a lot of conversations in the next couple of months. I'll actually, instead of going in joy for ball games this year, I'll go to some games along with Joe and he'll do the same thing, whether we'll go together or separate and talk to presidents and athletic directors and talk to athletes, get their input. the deadline for input that we sent that letter out with August 31st. But we'll, you know, that's just from the people that we sent letters to. We'll talk to hundreds of people. My staff will do the same thing. Joe Manchin's staff will do the same thing. We have lawyers on our staff. They will be talking to compliance. We'll be visiting with NCAA. There's a lot of groups out there. Athletic directors have formed committees that have been working on this for a year. They ran into a wall, but we want to find out, you know, we don't want to start in scratch if that makes sense. We want to get their input. So, okay, you've already done that. You don't think it'll work. Let's let us look into it, see if we can go a little bit different route. So, American Football Coast Association, I was president of it, what, six, seven years ago. I think that we can use their database, maybe have zoom calls with a lot of some of the coaches on Mondays, on an off day during the season. But we've got to have input for everybody. And again, players and parents don't be much as input as anybody. We want to get their thoughts about the first year and a half, two years of how this is shaken out and see the good and bad of what they've gone through. see what they suggest again. We don't have the answers. The answers will come from the people that actually already been there and their experiences.",
